{"name":"Speaking of the Devil","hex":"#a8415b","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"speaking of the devil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["An expression sometimes used when a person mentioned in the current conversation happens to arrive on the scene."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speaking_of_the_devil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Speaking of the Devil","blocks":[{"text":"Speaking of the Devil is a 1991 Italian comedy film directed by Enzo Barboni. It was the last collaboration between Barboni and Bud Spencer with the pairs sons co-writing the film together; Spencer's daughter also plays a role in the film."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Speaking-of-the-devil-poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speaking_of_the_Devil"},{"title":"Devil","blocks":[{"text":"The devil is a mythical personification of evil as conceived in various cultures and religious traditions. It is seen as the objectification of a hostile and destructive force. Jeffrey Burton Russell states that the different conceptions of the Devil can be summed up as 1. a principle of evil independent from God, 2. an aspect of God, 3. a created being turning evil or 4. a symbol of human evil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/022_devil_representation.JPG/330px-022_devil_representation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bf/Speaking-of-the-devil-poster.jpg/250px-Speaking-of-the-devil-poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Speaking-of-the-devil-poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi